  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\n   The current SLSQP local optimization is likely trapped in a local minimum. We need a global search method. Differential Evolution (DE) is chosen because it maintains a population of candidates and uses mutation/crossover to explore the space globally. This helps escape local minima and potentially finds the global minimum for C. The high-dimensional 140-variable space requires a global optimizer. We'll use DE with repair function to enforce integral and bounds constraints.\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n   - Variables: h(x) represented by 140 parameters for [0,1] domain\n   - Objective: Minimize C5 = max_k \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx\n   - Repair function: Ensures sum(h) = 70 (n_points/4) and bounds [0,1]\n   - Representation: n_half=140 variables for first half of domain, mirrored for full [0,2]\n   - DE strategy: 'best1' with mutation factor 0.7 and recombination rate 0.9\n   - Repair: Before each evaluation, repair candidate to ensure integral and bounds\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n   a. Initialize with parent solution if available\n   b. Define repair function that scales and clips candidate to enforce integral and bounds\n   c. Define objective function computing C5 after repair\n   d. Set DE bounds to [0,1]^140\n   e. Configure DE parameters (max_iter=20, popsize=20)\n   f. Run DE optimization while tracking best solution\n   g. Return best candidate after repair and compute final C5\n\n4. Search choices and variations:\n   - Population size: 20 to 40 for balance between exploration and execution time\n   - Mutation factor: 0.7 as balance between exploration and exploitation\n   - Strategy: 'best1' as good for unimodal optimization\n   - Time budget: Stop early if remaining evaluation time is insufficient\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness:\n   - Dominant cost: Objective eval (~100ms for 280-point convolution)\n   - DE evaluations: Limited by time budget (~500 evaluations in 100s)\n   - Check time remaining before each evaluation and skip if falling behind\n   - Graceful degradation: Fallback to parent solution if no progress\n\n6. Validation and return contract:\n   Uses same repair method as original code to ensure consistency:\n   - Stores best candidate during optimization\n   - Repairs final candidate before returning\n   - Returns tuple: (h_values, c5_bound, n_points)\n   - Ensures h_values length 280 and [0,1] bounds\n   - Computed C5 matches evaluation method",
